created_at: 2026-07-24T10:15:19.685057+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:1115b42c-b4ec-4a74-affb-9d2f09db206f] @ 2026-07-24T10:15:19.685057+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:b4448ae8-c0d3-4aca-a3ad-8598096b957a] @ 2026-07-24T10:15:19.685057+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:c282e44d-4e69-49ff-aafd-b8f233a012e7] @ 2026-07-24T10:15:19.685057+00:00

Content hash uses FNV-1a 64-bit (BigInt arithmetic, pure TS, no node:crypto) over fields joined with a control-character (U+0001) separator to avoid naive-concatenation field-boundary ambiguity. Hash output is a 16-hex-char string — a dedup fingerprint, not a cryptographic hash; node:crypto's SHA-256 was explicitly rejected per core-purity/dedup constraints.
