created_at: 2026-07-24T10:15:19.688337+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:1115b42c-b4ec-4a74-affb-9d2f09db206f] @ 2026-07-24T10:15:19.688337+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:b4448ae8-c0d3-4aca-a3ad-8598096b957a] @ 2026-07-24T10:15:19.688337+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:c282e44d-4e69-49ff-aafd-b8f233a012e7] @ 2026-07-24T10:15:19.688337+00:00

normalizeForHash strips Unicode combining diacritical marks (U+0300-U+036F) post-NFKD decomposition (e.g. 'café' -> matches 'cafe'). It does NOT transliterate non-combining distinct letters (e.g. Polish 'ł' does not decompose under NFKD and is NOT stripped) — a deliberate, documented limitation, not a bug.
