-> HAS_FACET [node:7343ff3d-c6d7-438f-b380-bd24640e1f74] @ 2026-07-24T10:15:19.700297+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:b4448ae8-c0d3-4aca-a3ad-8598096b957a] @ 2026-07-24T10:15:19.700297+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:c9b15b68-7ec3-414f-8782-9afd2436f208] @ 2026-07-24T10:15:19.700297+00:00

Env-var nesting keys (COFFER_<segment>__<segment>...) are matched CASE-SENSITIVELY against the JSON tree — the segment after each __ must spell the JSON key exactly. Env values are parsed JSON-first (JSON.parse) and fall back to the raw string on parse failure, so "true"->bool, "42"->number, arrays, and plain strings all work from one code path.
