-> HAS_FACET [node:611fe614-2e32-4e71-bca8-be7d434edfc6] @ 2026-07-24T10:15:19.739177+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:702ef151-2cc0-4464-8a36-f7c990329abe] @ 2026-07-24T10:15:19.739177+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:b4448ae8-c0d3-4aca-a3ad-8598096b957a] @ 2026-07-24T10:15:19.739177+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:c282e44d-4e69-49ff-aafd-b8f233a012e7] @ 2026-07-24T10:15:19.739177+00:00

runImportPipeline({parser, payload, ctx, store, batchId}) is deliberately narrow: parse -> normalizeTransaction (stamps importBatchId + contentHash) -> store.save(batchId, txns) -> return SaveResult. It does NOT call store.migrate() or store.createBatch() (composition-root concerns), and it has ZERO dedup logic of its own — StorePort.save() owns ALL dedup (within-batch AND cross-batch) via a UNIQUE constraint / Map key. This is a narrower, single-owner design than the plan's prose implied.
---
