-> HAS_FACET [node:b4448ae8-c0d3-4aca-a3ad-8598096b957a] @ 2026-07-24T10:22:47.920247+00:00

coffer-classification Rule model: a Rule's predicate is serializable DATA, not a JS function — a discriminated union of field matchers { field:'description'|'counterparty'|'amount'|'account', op, value } composed with all/any (AND/OR) combinators, so rules can be persisted and minted from corrections. Rule = { id, name?, order, predicate, assign: groupId[], stopAfter?:boolean }. The pure core engine evaluates a tx against ALL rules in `order`, accumulates the additive UNION of every matching rule's assign (not first-match); a matching rule with stopAfter halts further evaluation (exclusivity escape). Implements dec:6.
---
