P2 engine.ts classify(txns, rules) semantics settled: rules sorted ascending by order before evaluation regardless of input array order; per-tx a Set<groupId> dedups so two matching rules assigning the same group produce one Assignment (first rule's ruleId wins); stopAfter halts only that transaction's remaining rule evaluation, scoped per-tx not global. Zero matching rules -> zero assignments for that tx; 'unmatched' is not a value the pure engine returns, it's the caller/store's derived read (empty assignment set) per dec:efd6891c, deferred to P3.
