P3 implemented: ClassificationStorePort extended with upsertRule/listRules/saveAssignments/assignmentsFor/unmatched(contentHashes). saveAssignments is the single write path for every source and is INSERT-OR-IGNORE-semantics on (txContentHash, groupId) in both the SQLite adapter (UNIQUE constraint) and the in-memory fake (first-writer-wins Map) -- this alone gives sticky-manual (a rule row can never overwrite an existing manual row for the same pair) and idempotent re-eval, with zero special-casing in the orchestrator. unmatched() takes a caller-supplied candidate content-hash list rather than querying a transactions table it doesn't own, since ClassificationStorePort never owns Transaction data (dec:a49130e3) -- core/classify/run.ts's reviewQueue() computes the actual Transaction[] by filtering the caller's txns against that hash set. Shared contract extended with a seedTransactions hook so assignment/rule tests can satisfy the SQLite adapter's real FK (assignments -> transactions, assignments -> groups, assignments -> rules) while the in-memory fake ignores it (no FK to satisfy).
---
