P4 implemented: core/classify/promote.ts (pure derivePredicate + promoteToRule; id/order are caller-supplied since pure core cannot mint ids or read a store's next-order) and core/classify/correction.ts (recordManualCorrection + promoteCorrectionToRule, both store-touching orchestration over ClassificationStorePort only). Deliberately does NOT re-run the engine itself -- the caller (composition root, P6) calls runClassification again after promoting, so the new rule's effect applies uniformly to the whole transaction set, not just the originating tx. Tests prove: promoted rule reproduces the correction on a DIFFERENT matching transaction; re-eval after promotion leaves the original manual row's source unchanged; two consecutive re-evals produce no duplicate rows and do not disturb an unrelated manual correction on a different transaction.
