-> CONTRADICTS [node:bc0ab42f-9e20-4780-85df-748975ff1d1c] @ 2026-07-24T11:02:01.496600+00:00

coffer-analytics partition v1 = designated-primary-group-else-EVEN; the 'by split amounts' branch of the two-mode attribution decision is DEFERRED. Slices 1-2 persist no split table and no split-amount field (engine.ts / assignment.ts Assignment = {txContentHash, groupId, source, ruleId?}, no amount), so partition cannot resolve by split amounts without a new split model + migration. 'Primary' is NOT a new persisted field either: partition takes an optional PURE policy primaryGroupOf(txHash, candidateGroups)=>groupId? in opts, default none -> even. Even-split distributes the amount.minor bigint across N groups with a deterministic remainder (+1 minor unit to first |minor%N| groups by sorted groupId), so a tx's partition sums to its amount EXACTLY. This narrows bc0ab42f openly, not silently: the split branch is a known deferral, even/primary remain exact.
