-> HAS_FACET [node:7bf33f0b-9017-4f19-9dac-fd91f332de6b] @ 2026-07-24T11:19:57.389967+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:7dbff5bf-286e-4f4a-929a-c13e11b953c3] @ 2026-07-24T11:19:57.389967+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:ac2535ce-0454-406e-ad95-c3a1689c994f] @ 2026-07-24T11:20:04.655483+00:00

Deterministic bigint even-split remainder rule (coffer-analytics attribution.ts evenSplit): splitting a signed bigint `total` across `n` ids sorted ascending gives each id `total/n` (bigint truncating division), then distributes the |total % n| leftover minor units one-each, sign-aware (+1 in the direction of total's sign), to the first |remainder| ids by sorted id. Property-tested: the parts always sum EXACTLY to `total`, including n > |total| (many parts of value 0) and negative totals. Generalizable pattern for any future exact-bigint-split-across-N-keys problem — sort keys deterministically, base = total/n, remainder = total%n, walk sorted keys assigning +/-1 while remainder count > 0.
---
