-> DEPENDS_ON [node:eed7cc3c-fbcf-4c5b-886b-66d25d867389] @ 2026-07-24T11:20:04.657747+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:ef7fd20e-eb69-4bb6-9cb1-36ea33eece71] @ 2026-07-24T11:19:57.397833+00:00

coffer-analytics timezone-free date bucketing rule (buckets.ts): ISO 'YYYY-MM-DD' strings are parsed by splitting into y/m/d integers and building a UTC-midnight epoch via Date.UTC — NEVER `new Date(localString)` and never a local get*() accessor, only getUTC*() ones, to avoid host-timezone drift. day bucket = the date itself; week bucket = start of the ISO week (Monday, computed via (getUTCDay()+6)%7 offset); month bucket = first-of-month (Date.UTC(y,m,1)). Every bucket key is rendered back to 'YYYY-MM-DD' via getUTCFullYear/getUTCMonth/getUTCDate. Reusable pattern for any future core module needing calendar bucketing without a timezone/date library.
---
