coffer-analytics (slice 3 of coffer-mvp) reviewed at gw-review: core/analytics/{model,buckets,cashflow,attribution,by-group,series}.ts, pure/zero-I/O, ClassificationStorePort.allAssignments() bulk read (SQLite adapter + in-memory fake + shared contract, both tested), Container.analytics() join method. Verified independently: pnpm typecheck 464 files/0 errors, pnpm test 293 passed/1 skipped (31 files), pnpm build green, boundary-lint clean (core/analytics imports only relative core/model + ./ siblings, no ports/adapters/d3/layerchart). attribute()'s per-tx partition reconciliation (even-split bigint remainder, primary-else-even) is CONFIRMED exact including negative amounts and n>|minor| via a 200-trial property sweep and a mandatory primary-branch test. by-group rollup subtree-dedup CONFIRMED (no parent+child double count). CAVEAT for slice 4: byGroupSeriesSets()'s DTO-level claim that a partition SeriesSet's series sum EXACTLY to grandTotalMinor is FALSE whenever the currency has any unclassified (zero-assignment) transaction — attribute() silently skips those, but grandTotalMinor sums ALL txns. No test covers the mixed assigned/unassigned case. Captured as issue [node] CONTRADICTS-linked to the settled reconciliation constraint 336cd92d — slice 4 must resolve (surface an 'unclassified' bucket, or re-scope grandTotalMinor to classified-only, or re-test/re-word the constraint) before shipping a chart that implies exact reconciliation. Verdict: Approve with a flagged follow-up, not a blocker for merge (core logic and tests for the shipped scope are sound) but MUST be addressed before/alongside slice-4 UI work that renders partition totals.
