Coffer ships a minimal single-passphrase authentication gate (amended 2026-07-24, supersedes the accepted gap 'reverse-proxy auth is the user's concern'): passphrase from the config layer (COFFER_AUTH__PASSWORD), server-side verification, signed session cookie, ALL routes gated, login screen in the design system and i18n'd. Reason: the dogfood deployment is public (coffer.rashell.pl); hosting PoW/WAF complements but does not replace app auth. Multi-user accounts remain out of scope.
