-> DEPENDS_ON [node:eb704b61-26ef-4a0d-b392-418df1d5352f] @ 2026-07-24T14:31:29.960163+00:00

coffer-ui-i18n picks the HAND-ROLLED TYPED CATALOG over @inlang/paraglide-js (both permitted by dec:10/eb704b61). i18n lives in src/lib/i18n/: messages/{en,pl}.ts as Record<MessageKey,string|((p)=>string)> keyed off ONE shared MessageKey union, so a missing pl key is a typecheck FAILURE (stronger than paraglide's runtime-missing behaviour); a tiny t(key,params) reader + a Svelte-5 rune locale store; format.ts wrapping Intl.NumberFormat/currency/DateTimeFormat (this is the real money DISPLAY formatter that core's formatMoney [node:4f66243c] deliberately is NOT). Why not paraglide: its vite build-plugin + generated src/lib/paraglide dir + its own SvelteKit locale handle would have to be sequenced with the new auth handle and RUN before every pnpm typecheck/vitest, adding friction to the pnpm-only, jsdom, no-browser substrate for a 4-screen en+pl surface. Tripwire back to paraglide: message count explodes or ICU pluralization becomes required.
---
