no-hardcoded-strings guard (src/test/no-hardcoded-strings.test.ts) required two regex-scanner fixes beyond the naive boundary-lint-style approach: (1) HTML comments <!--...--> must be stripped before scanning or developer prose in comments false-positives; (2) Svelte {..} expressions must be stripped via a manual BALANCED-brace scan (not a `/\{[^{}]*\}/` regex) because nested object-literal params (e.g. `{t(locale,'x',{name:userName})}`) and inline arrow-function attrs (e.g. `onkeydown={(e)=>select(id)}`, whose `=>` contains a bare `>`) both break single-level regex stripping and a naive `<[^>]*>` tag-strip respectively. Correct order: strip script/style/comments -> scan quoted attr literals (title/aria-label/placeholder/alt) on that markup -> balanced-strip {..} expressions -> THEN strip tags -> scan remaining text-node lines. Verified via seeded-violation fixtures (text node + aria-label) plus a negative fixture asserting t() calls, bound expressions, data-testid/aria-hidden/id, brand 'Coffer', and bare punctuation are never flagged.
