coffer-ui-i18n P5 (auth gate) implemented: src/lib/server/auth/{constants,passphrase,secret,session,login,handle,runtime,index}.ts. verifyPassphrase: SHA-256 digest + timingSafeEqual, fail-closed on missing auth.password. createSecretResolver(): factory (not module singleton) resolving auth.secret/COFFER_AUTH__SECRET; throws in production when unset, generates+caches a random per-boot dev secret with a console.warn otherwise ([node:512a3d11] satisfied). issueSession/verifySession: HMAC-SHA256 signed coffer_session cookie `<base64url payload>.<hex sig>`; tamper rejection required an explicit string-length check on the hex signature BEFORE Buffer.from(str,'hex') decoding — Node's hex decoder silently truncates at the first invalid pair, so appending garbage to a valid signature decoded to the SAME bytes and passed timingSafeEqual undetected. Caught by an added regression test, fixed with a pre-decode length check. createAuthHandle (src/lib/server/auth/handle.ts) gates all routes via unauthenticatedResponse: /api/** or non-GET or non-text/html-Accept -> 401; browser HTML GET -> redirect(303,'/login'); /login + /_app/* + favicon/robots exempt. src/hooks.server.ts composes sequence(localeHandle-passthrough, authHandle) — locale slot left as an explicit passthrough for P2/P4 to fill. src/routes/login/+page.server.ts (form action via attemptLogin) + +page.svelte (minimal, but wired to the REAL P2 catalog keys auth.loginTitle/loginSubtitle/passphraseLabel/loginError/loginButton via t('en', key) — P2 had already landed those keys ahead of P5, so the placeholder used real i18n instead of raw hardcoded text) + src/routes/logout/+server.ts (POST clears cookie, redirects /login). AppConfig extended with auth: { password?: string; secret?: string } in config.port.ts + "auth": {} in config/default.json. Gotcha: ConfigPort.get(path, defaultValue) throws when defaultValue is explicitly undefined (treated the same as 'no default') — used config.getAll().auth?.password/.secret instead of get() for the optional auth fields. Verification: pnpm typecheck 0 errors; boundary-lint green; all 5 new auth test files (34 tests) green. Remaining pnpm test failures are pre-existing/out-of-scope: P1 design-system jsdom-mount errors (Button/ModeLabel/Table/ThemeToggle) and the root placeholder src/routes/+page.svelte hardcoded text (P4's to replace) — not touched, not caused by this phase.
