vite.config.ts required a minimal but UNAVOIDABLE edit for coffer-ui-i18n P1's jsdom component tests to run: a per-file `// @vitest-environment jsdom` pragma only swaps vitest's JS-global environment, NOT which Svelte build `import { mount } from 'svelte'` resolves to. Root cause chased in installed source (Vite 8.1.5 Environment API + @sveltejs/vite-plugin-svelte 7.2.0's compile.js `this.environment.config.consumer === 'server'` check): SvelteKit's own resolve.conditions wins over vite-plugin-svelte's per-environment client defaults unless something puts 'browser' ahead of 'node'. Fix: added `test.projects` to vite.config.ts (component: environment jsdom + `svelteTesting()` plugin from `@testing-library/svelte/vite`, already a devDep; server: environment node, same include/exclude split by src/lib/ui/**). Smallest correct fix on this stack; no alternative (pragma alone, environmentMatchGlobs) works for Svelte-5-under-SvelteKit jsdom component tests here.
