coffer-ui-i18n (slice 4 of coffer-mvp) reviewed at gw-review, GREEN, Approve: BG/Forgotten-Realms 4-screen SvelteKit UI (dashboard/import/review/settings) over slices 1-3, hand-rolled typed i18n catalog (en+pl, 37+ keys, fantasy register chrome-only, missing-key = typecheck failure), single-passphrase auth gate on ALL routes (incl /api, fail-closed on missing password AND missing prod secret, constant-time compare, HMAC-signed HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite=Lax session cookie), bigint<->decimal-string DTO boundary (minorToString/stringToMinor, the ONLY converters, Number() only at the chart/format display edge), and hand-rolled SVG charts (layerchart 2.0.2 installed but not wired — disclosed drift, see the sibling tripwire-honesty issue node) rendering the __unclassified__ series distinctly with AttributionMode always labeled. P6 integration phase found and fixed three real deploy-blocking bugs (case-insensitive env-var matching, sqlite parent-dir mkdir on first boot, migrations bundled via Vite ?raw instead of readdirSync) that slice 5 (packaging) directly consumes. Verified independently at review: pnpm typecheck 573 files/0 errors/4 non-blocking Svelte-reactivity warnings; pnpm test 47 files/385 passed/1 skipped; pnpm build green under production auth env vars; a live fresh-boot smoke test on PORT=4179 confirmed fail-closed 401 on unauth non-HTML/API, 303->/login on unauth browser GET, 401 on wrong passphrase, 303+properly-flagged cookie on correct passphrase, and all four screens 200 once authenticated. WCAG AA contrast independently recomputed for 9 token pairs (light+dark, text and data-positive/negative/unclassified), all clear with margin (5.67:1-14.66:1). i18n register sampled 6 keys both languages, consistent. No-hardcoded-string guard's exclusion list read critically — not over-broad (structural attrs, non-alpha text, one brand allowlist entry). Two disputed nodes from slice 3 (bdfeb7e7/336cd92d, the partition-reconciliation-vs- unclassified-txns gap) are effectively addressed by this slice's rendering of the __unclassified__ series, but remain in the review queue pending explicit human resolution — not auto-resolved by this review. Slice 5 (packaging) is next and directly consumes the deploy-hardening constraints captured this cycle.
